<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <queries>
        <intent>
            <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />

            <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
        </intent>
    </queries>

    <!--
        Backup is OFF, deliberately, and both attributes below say so because they cover
        different transports: allowBackup governs cloud backup (and the pre-31 path), while
        dataExtractionRules governs Android 12+ cloud backup and device-to-device transfer.
        Turning off only the first would still let a device transfer carry the data across.

        The reason is that SlowLock's stored state is not portable. A lock exists exactly when
        its shortcut is pinned (FR-003a), the pinned shortcuts live in the launcher and do not
        travel with a backup, and LockStore's list is only the ORDER those rows were last seen
        in. Restoring that list onto a new phone would seed the Locks screen from a launcher
        that holds none of the shortcuts it describes. There is nothing here worth carrying and
        a restore is strictly worse than a fresh start.
    -->
    <application
        android:name=".SlowLockApplication"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:dataExtractionRules="@xml/data_extraction_rules"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.SlowLock">
        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:label="@string/app_name"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.SlowLock"
            android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />

                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

        <!--
            The target of every pinned shortcut, and now the wait screen
            (003-launch-delay/contracts/wait-screen.md). Its android:name is FROZEN - it is
            written into each shortcut's persisted intent (contracts/pinned-shortcut.md), and
            ShortcutContractTest fails the build if the class ever moves.

            exported="false" is correct and deliberate: the launcher does not start this
            intent itself, it calls LauncherApps.startShortcut() and the system starts the
            intent under SlowLock's own identity, so no export is needed (002 research.md R5).

            excludeFromRecents and the empty taskAffinity are unchanged from feature 002 and
            still carry FR-031: no SlowLock entry in recents, and the target opens in its own
            task so backing out of it does not unwind into the wait screen.

            Two changes this feature makes, both deliberate:

            - theme: Theme.SlowLock.Invisible -> Theme.SlowLock.Wait. The activity is now MEANT
              to be seen, and its windowBackground is the colour WaitScreen paints, so the tap
              lands on the final background with no flash (003 research.md R7).
            - noHistory="true" is REMOVED. It finishes the activity on every onStop - INCLUDING
              a rotation - which would restart the wait each time the device turned. The
              explicit onStop rule (obligation W15, US4) has the isChangingConfigurations
              exception that noHistory cannot express (003 research.md R5).

            launchMode="singleTop" is new: a second tap of the same shortcut must arrive at
            onNewIntent and be ignored, not start a second wait (obligation W22, FR-027).
        -->
        <activity
            android:name=".shortcut.ShortcutLaunchActivity"
            android:exported="false"
            android:excludeFromRecents="true"
            android:launchMode="singleTop"
            android:taskAffinity=""
            android:theme="@style/Theme.SlowLock.Wait" />
    </application>

</manifest>